!scripts/bookfunnel_books.json
!scripts/audit_exclusions.json
# Hand-placed ebook covers (scripts/build_ebook_manifest cover source 3). MUST
# be tracked: it is build input, so an untracked copy would give this machine
# covers that CI and every other checkout silently lack.
!scripts/ebook_cover_overrides.json
!last_catalog_snapshot.json
# The cross-language slug pin. MUST be tracked: tests/test_shelf_map.py and
# site/__tests__/shelf-link.test.js BOTH read it, so an untracked copy is two
# suites that pass on this machine and fail in CI on a missing file. Holds book
# titles and their slugs only — the same strings the public catalogue already
# serves — so it is safe in a public repo.
!tests/fixtures/slug_cases.json
# ⚠️ site/shelf_book_map.json has NO negation and is nonetheless tracked (it was
# force-added). A tracked file bypasses .gitignore, so `git check-ignore` calls
# it clean and a future session will not find a rule explaining why it works.
# Regenerated by scripts/build_shelf_map.py; if it is ever untracked, it needs a
# negation here rather than another -f.
!site/chapters.json
!site/discussion_prompts.json
!site/content_warnings.json
!site/additions_log.json
# The hand-reviewed cross-catalog joins. MUST be tracked, for three reasons at
# once: deploy.yml assembles each lane from that branch's COMMITTED site/, so an
# untracked copy is a 404 and a modal that silently loses its links;
# tests/test_cross_catalog_overrides.py and site/__tests__/library-link.test.js
# BOTH read it, so an untracked copy is two suites that pass here and fail in
# CI; and library_catalog reads it out of this checkout, so a clone without it
# cannot run `npm run check:cross-links`. Holds book titles and library work
# ids only — strings the public catalogue already serves.
!site/cross-catalog-overrides.json
# ⚠️ site/ebooks.json IS DELIBERATELY NOT NEGATED — it was, until 2026-08-17.
# Owner directive: "ebooks should be like the other site where we grant
# permission to view it. I don't want people scraping my books." Two public
# surfaces had to close, and closing only one would have moved a door in front
# of an open window:
#   1. the Pages deployment (deploy.yml assembles _site/ from each branch's
#      committed site/, so a tracked manifest shipped to
#      audiobooks.heygabi.ai/ebooks.json), and
#   2. ⚠️ THIS REPO, which is PUBLIC and must stay public (it is the only repo
#      with workflows; two crons would exhaust metered Actions minutes on a
#      private one). A tracked file here is world-readable at a stable raw URL
#      no matter what the site serves.
# The manifest is still WRITTEN to site/ by sync step 1b and every local check
# still reads it — it simply never leaves this machine except through
# scripts/publish_ebooks_manifest.py, into the PRIVATE `ebooks-gated` R2
# bucket, behind apps/audiobook-worker's GET /api/ebooks/manifest.
# ⚠️ Do not "fix" this by re-adding the negation. site/covers_manifest.json
# below stays negated: it is a list of sha256 hashes, not a list of books.
site/ebooks.json
# ⚠️ The ONE ebook file that stays public and TRACKED: freshness only.
# `site/ebooks_status.json` = {generated_at, count, needs_human_cover_count}.
# The apex /status page and the estate probe suite read it to answer "did sync
# step 1b run?" — a question that must not require handing an admin page the
# whole shelf. ⚠️ Counts and times only: no titles, no authors, no paths, and
# never the needs_human_cover ENTRIES, which name files. Adding a field that
# identifies a book reopens, in this one file, the surface the gate closed.
!site/ebooks_status.json
# The publish receipt (which sha256 is in the bucket) — machine-local state,
# like the covers upload's own bookkeeping.
scripts/.ebooks_published.json
# The docs-snapshot publisher's own bookkeeping (scripts/publish_docs_snapshot.py,
# GABI docs assistant phase 1) and its upload scratch directory. Same reasoning as
# the line above — machine-local state, plus a temp copy of the gzipped corpus.
# ⚠️ The state file lists every INCLUDED doc path so the next run can print a
# +files/-files diff; several of those paths are audiobook_catalog's own
# LOCAL-ONLY docs, so it must never become tracked in this PUBLIC repo.
scripts/.docs_published.json
scripts/.docs_snapshot_tmp/
# ⚠️ site/ebook_files_manifest.json IS DELIBERATELY NOT NEGATED EITHER, and the
# reason is the same one as site/ebooks.json above. It is the record of which
# ebook FILES are in the private `estate-ebooks` bucket (viewer phase 0a,
# scripts/upload_ebooks_r2.py) and it is keyed on FILE PATHS — i.e. it is a
# list of the household's books by name, which is exactly the surface the gate
# closed. `*.json` above already ignores it; this comment exists so nobody
# "helpfully" adds a negation. ⚠️ This is a deliberate deviation from
# library_catalog/docs/info/ebook-viewer-design.md §2.1, which said "committed"
# — see docs/info/ebooks-r2-ingest.md §3. Nothing off this machine needs it:
# the phase-1a Worker resolves anchor -> path from ebooks.json in the gated
# bucket, never from this record. site/covers_manifest.json stays negated
# because it is a list of sha256 hashes, not a list of books.
# (tests/test_upload_ebooks_r2.py fails if a negation is added.)
# ⚠️ site/audio_manifest.json IS DELIBERATELY NOT NEGATED, third of its kind.
# The record of which AUDIOBOOK files are in the private `estate-audio` bucket
# (audio-player phase 0b, scripts/upload_audio_r2.py), keyed on FILE PATHS —
# the same "list of the household's books by name" surface as the two above,
# and 630 GB of it. `*.json` already ignores it; this comment exists so nobody
# adds a negation. ⚠️ Note the asymmetry that IS correct: site/chapters.json
# stays PUBLIC and negated by owner decision 2026-08-17 ("fine as is") —
# chapter TITLES are published, audio BYTES and the paths to them are not.
# (tests/test_upload_audio_r2.py fails if a negation is added.)
!site/covers_manifest.json
!vitest.config.js
!firebase.json
scripts/upload_manifest.json
scripts/token.json
scripts/credentials.json
node_modules/

# Generated site outputs (rebuilt locally, committed for Pages deployment)
# site/index.html — committed (needed for GitHub Pages)
# site/catalog.csv — committed (needed for GitHub Pages)
# site/stats.html — committed (needed for GitHub Pages)
#
# ⚠️⚠️ NEVER gitignore site/ itself, or site/index.html / site/catalog.csv /
# site/static. Doing that once caused a full site outage, and
# .github/workflows/promote.yml's first guard refuses to promote if any of
# them is ignored. That guard is correct and stays.
#
# site/covers/ IS the one sanctioned exception, added 2026-08-10. Cover art
# (243 MB / 1,843 files) now lives in Cloudflare R2 and the site links
# straight at the bucket, so the images are no longer a deploy artifact — they
# were being copied into BOTH lanes on every deploy (~514 MB per publish).
# site/covers/ is still produced locally by app/writers.py; it is the upload
# source for scripts/upload_covers_r2.py, not something to ship.
#
# The committed replacement is site/covers_manifest.json (negated above) —
# the record of what is in the bucket, and what the promote audit checks
# instead of statting files. Removing site/covers from that promote guard had
# to land in the SAME commit as this line; splitting them breaks the next
# promote. See catalog-platform/docs/DOMAIN_AND_HOSTING.md §2.6(a) and
# docs/info/covers-r2.md.
site/covers/

