# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
# ⚠️ EXCEPT the vendored pdf.js renderer, whose upstream layout happens to use
# the name `build/` (viewer phase 1b, 2026-08-17). The Python `build/` rule
# above matched `site/static/pdfjs/build/` and SILENTLY dropped both renderer
# files from a `git add site/static/pdfjs` — caught only because the commit was
# checked file-by-file. Shipping that would have deployed a reader page whose
# renderer 404s, i.e. a book that never opens, with nothing in any test or
# build log to say why. tests/test_reader_page.py now asserts these are TRACKED
# IN GIT rather than merely present on disk, which is the check that would have
# caught it on its own.
!site/static/pdfjs/build/
!site/static/pdfjs/build/*.js
